# architecture.mdc — YAML schema (template — not live config)

> **Bootstrap:** On `start`, the orchestrator **reads the repo** and **generates** `.cursor/project-context/architecture.mdc` with real `summary`, `layers[].paths`, `integrations`, etc. See [project-context-bootstrap.md](../../sdlc-system/workflow/project-context-bootstrap.md) § `architecture.mdc`.

```yaml
architecture:
  summary: TBD  # bootstrap: one paragraph from README + codebase — what THIS system does

  style: modular-monolith  # bootstrap: infer from repo layout

  layers:
    - name: http
      paths: []  # bootstrap: list real paths — controllers, routes, handlers, api/
    - name: business
      paths: []  # bootstrap: services, domain, use-cases, core logic
    - name: infrastructure
      paths: []  # bootstrap: repositories, clients, adapters, messaging

  boundaries: []

  integrations: []

  auth:
    userFacingPattern: TBD
    partnerPattern: TBD
    configPaths: []

  errorHandling:
    businessException: TBD
    codes: []

  diagrams:
    existing: []
    preferredFormat: mermaid

  repositoryRelationships:
    - primary: <org>/<repo>
      consumes: []
```
